COMPATPROBE(1)

NAME
    compatprobe - test BusyBox-facing compatibility paths

SYNOPSIS
    compatprobe

DESCRIPTION
    compatprobe is a guest regression probe for the Unix compatibility layer.
    It checks the pieces that BusyBox and POSIX-shaped programs commonly touch:
    /bin/sh, /proc directory and file reads, /dev/null, /dev/zero, statfs,
    sysinfo, metadata updates, truncate, hard links, symbolic links, readlink,
    lstat, mknod, mkfifo, and related libc wrappers.

    The probe is installed under /usr/libexec/tests and is normally run by the
    host-driven selftest suite rather than by hand.

SEE ALSO
    busybox(1), selftest(1), shell(1)
